<LegalLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Information about browser storage, external website services, and the current use of analytics and advertising technologies on the Belaro Precision website." updated="2026-11-27" updatedLabel="November 27, 2026">
  <h2>1. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small pieces of information stored by a browser. Similar technologies include local storage and session storage. These are distinct from ordinary requests used to load a page, font or image, which can still disclose technical information such as an IP address to a service provider.</p>
  <h2>2. Current website functionality</h2>
  <p>The enquiry form saves the basic contact details you enter (name, business email, company, country or region, and phone / WhatsApp calling code and number) in this browser's local storage so they can be restored on another page. The saved values remain on this device until the browser site data is cleared or replaced by later form input; project descriptions, consent choices and drawings are not stored there. The form sends information to our form service only when you submit it. If browser storage is unavailable, the form still works without cross-page prefill. Optional advertising attribution storage is described below.</p>
  <p>After a comment is submitted, its name and email are saved in this browser's local storage for future comments. The comment text is not stored there. You can remove these details by clearing this website's browser data; commenting still works if browser storage is unavailable.</p>
  <p>The live chat script from wsdesk.geekmt.com loads on each page. It uses this website’s local storage for a visitor session identifier, conversation status, read status and pending messages so the conversation can continue across pages and pending messages can be retried. These entries use a relaydesk.livechat prefix. The browser contacts the chat service when the script loads, even before you open the chat. Clearing this storage may prevent you from resuming an earlier conversation; it does not delete messages already sent to us.</p>
  <p>Hosting and security services may process technical request information and may use necessary security technologies depending on their configuration. When enabled on the enquiry and comment forms, Cloudflare Turnstile processes browser signals to help detect automated abuse. Its behaviour may vary with the security configuration. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>3. Fonts and images</h2>
  <p>Page images are served from this website. Google Fonts are loaded from external servers, which causes your browser to contact Google; an external font request is not itself evidence of an advertising cookie. For more information, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>4. Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>When a page address contains a valid Google Ads click identifier, we ask before saving it. If you allow this, belaro.ad-attribution in local storage holds the available gclid, gbraid or wbraid identifiers and a capture timestamp for up to 30 days, and these identifiers accompany your next enquiry. A new advertising click replaces the earlier record; ordinary visits do not extend its expiry. Expired records are removed on the next website visit or enquiry submission.</p>
  <p>belaro.ad-attribution-consent remembers your allow or decline choice for up to 180 days. Use Advertising preferences in the footer to change it. Declining or withdrawing clears the browser attribution record and prevents these identifiers from accompanying future enquiries. Already submitted enquiries are not deleted. If browser storage is unavailable, the form still works without these identifiers.</p>
  <p>When enabled, Google Tag Manager may load tags for analytics or advertising. The Advertising preferences control described here applies only to our click-identifier storage and its inclusion with an enquiry; it does not control Google Analytics, Google Ads tags, remarketing or live chat. Saving identifiers with an enquiry does not itself send a conversion to Google Ads.</p>
  <h2>5. Your browser controls</h2>
  <p>You can use your browser’s privacy settings to inspect, block or delete cookies and site data. The steps depend on the browser. Blocking security features or external resources may affect live chat, the enquiry form or page appearance. Deleting browser data does not delete an enquiry already sent to us.</p>
  <h2>6. Further information</h2>
  <p>Read our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for enquiry data, technical files and information requests. If you have questions about a browser request or stored item associated with this website, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> with the page and service involved.</p>
</LegalLayout>
